==Variants==
{{Variant
|original = Hippoe
|Metal Hippoe
|Hippoe's [[:Category:Metal Enemies|Metal]] variant, and the first Metal enemy encountered in the game. In terms of stats it is one of the weakest, but its Metal trait allows it to take a beating from anything that isn't a [[Critical Hit]].
|Super Metal Hippoe
|A much faster and stronger version of Metal Hippoe. He has a whopping 16 knockbacks and high health for a Metal enemy, with a 100% chance to knockback cats on hit.
|Lione Hippoe
|An enemy introduced in the [[Happy New Year? (Monthly Event)|Happy New Year?]] event (January event).
|Heavenly Hippoe
|Hippoe's [[:Category:Angel Enemies|Angel]] variant. He has high stats and rapid attacks.
|Hyppoh
|[[:Category:Alien Enemies|Alien]] version of Hippoe. She is much stronger and has longer range than Hippoe, though not as dangerous as Heavenly Hippoe.
|Zomboe
|[[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombie]] variant of Hippoe. It has 40x as much health and damage as Hippoe, slightly longer range, and 30% chance to slow cats for 4 seconds. Like most Zombies, it can also burrow under cats and revive once with 50% HP.
|Gold Hippoe
|An enemy that originates in [[GOLD RUSH#The Midas Touch|The Midas Touch]], with increased health, damage, range, and movement speed. He can freeze cats, and drops a lot of money when killed.
|Super Hyppoh
|An Alien/[[:Category:Colossus Enemies|Colossal]] variant of Hyppoh introduced in [[Horrorpotamus]]. She has a whopping 20 knockbacks, 100% chance to slow cats for 2 seconds, high damage, good health and despite her meager 222 standing range, has an Omni Strike that hits up to 350. Starts out weak, but receives massive buffs in later stages.
}}

