==Trivia==
*Hippoe's name may be derived from ''hippo'' and ''foe'' or any name ending in "oe", such as ''Joe'', ''Monroe'', ''Poe'', ''Zoe'', or even some names from Greek mythology such as ''[[wikipedia:Ocyrhoe|Ocyrhoe]]'', the name of a naiad-nymph who had a son named [[wikipedia:Hippomedon|Hippomedon]].
*Hippoe's Japanese name, Kaba-chan (カバちゃん), has a double meaning: while ''kaba'' (カバ) is Japanese for "hippopotamus", Kaba-chan is also the name of a [[wikipedia:Kaba-chan|transgender actress and choreographer]].
*Prior to [[Version 14.7 Update|Version 14.7]], Hippoe's description was:
<pre>
This dangerous hippo has
confidence in its stamina and power.
(s)he? has a multi attack skill.
We don't know if it is a he or a she.
</pre>
**Despite their old description saying otherwise, Hippoe does not have a "[[Multi-Hit|multi attack]] skill". This is likely a result of poor localization, as the original Japanese description specifies "attacking multiple bodies at once", presumably referring to Hippoe's Area Attacks.
*Although Hippoe's gender is unknown in [[The Battle Cats]], their description in the first English version, [[Battle Cats (Removed Game)|Battle Cats]], referred to them as female, stating "This dangerous Bi-sexual hippo has confidence in stamina and power. ''She'' has multi-attack skill."
**[[Hyppoh]]'s description also uses she/her, which could imply that both are the same hippo. However, the phrasing of her description suggests them to be entirely separate entities.
*Hippoe is listed as a source for the information in [[Bun Bun Symbiote]]'s description.
*The line, "A dangerous guy who attacks multiple units at once," (一度に複数体をまとめて攻撃してくる危険なやつ) in Hippoe's Japanese description was reused for [[Mr. Mer]]'s description in [[Kumanchu Royale]].
*Hippoe is the first enemy to appear as a boss and the first enemy to have [[Area Attack]].
*One of the possible endings for [[Gamatoto Expedition]] log messages is "with a Hippoe."
*One of the possible [[Cat Shrine#Cat Fortune|Cat Fortunes]] is "You'll lose to a Hippoe."

